    "analysis": "<p>PostgreSQL uses subtransactions (SAVEPOINT) for nested exception handling, frequently generated by ORMs such as Django and ActiveRecord. When active subtransactions exceed 64 per session (PGPROC_MAX_CACHED_SUBXIDS), PostgreSQL spills subtransactions from thread-local cache to shared memory (PGPROC) and disk (pg_subtrans).</p><p>This causes SubtransSLRU lock contention. Simultaneously, tuple lock lookups degrade from fast local cache checks to full SLRU reads under high concurrency, creating extreme lock acquisition spikes and database connection pool exhaustion.</p>",
